    // Issue #223: the climb of the cake and the way down it in level anti-gravity zones (#215): a
    // kart neither slows down going up nor speeds up going down. The climb (34 %) starts past the
    // trick ramp's landing and ends 30 m before the hairpin at the top; the way back down (17 %),
    // after the lacets, ends 31 m before the tight corner (a zone right before a hairpin sends the
    // pack over its wall: each bump between two karts is a spin boost in a zone). The way down
    // from the drop to the lacets stays gentle (5.6 %): its run-out takes most of it.
    anti_gravity: [
        (from: 37.0, to: 44.0),
        (from: 118.0, to: 127.0),
    ],
    // Issue #180 (GD § 16, rule 3): bumps, a real rise and fall of the road, 2.2 m high (a kart and
    // its driver), 30 m long: on the approach of the bulge (its trick lands well before the bulge,
    // whose first turn is gentle) and out of the last corner, before the grid (as on Prairie
    // Pompon). Not on the straights between two hairpins (one lands too late to prepare the drift),
